  <prompt>Extend RuleSetService and RuleSetEndpoints for the four scope levels (notes/rule-set-scope-design.md sections 4.1-4.6 and 5.1, as revised by uac-r2's review, section 12): validate scope and core record on create, assign and publish; require Read and AppendTo on a named core record; on every route keyed by the rule-set id, read the set's core record on the server and check the caller's Read (plus AppendTo on writes) before anything is read back or written, answering one uniform 404; lock a Published set's scope (409 ruleset.scope_locked); re-scope a Draft through ReparentAsync on the set and SecureChildReconciler.AfterRefileAsync; write the business-unit list; route the set, policy and version creates through IRecordOwnershipResolver with each row's own lookups as parents; and add sprk_ruleset to the secure family in ONE change (lineage with entity set sprk_rulesets, OwnershipParentEntities, the role row with a live refusal probe, sprk_createdbyperson on the three tables, census Routed entries and PersonBearingWriters, the NFR-05 depth check), with the narrower guard and its ontology twin. Send uac-r2 the citing lookups its delete planner reads (D-141).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, the Finance authorization filter, IRecordOwnershipResolver, SecureChildReconciler and the uac-r2 secure-family model.</role>

  <goal>A record-scoped rule set can be created, assigned and published only with a valid scope and core record and with the caller's Read + AppendTo on it; no route keyed by a rule-set id reveals or changes a set whose core record the caller cannot read; a Draft re-scope off a Secure record passes F3 and moves the set's rows; the set, policies and versions are owned through the resolver from their own lookups (Secure team under a Secure record); sprk_ruleset is in the lineage, the ownership parents, the role set, the creator-person set and the census in one change, with SecureFamilyConsistencyTests, the census, RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests and RouteAuthorizationGuardTests passing; the NFR-05 run reports no non-admin role reaching the Secure business unit on the three tables; uac-r2 has the citing lookups.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design note sections 4.1-4.6, 5.1, 5.3, 12 (ontology-r1 conditions 1-2; uac-r2 review items 1-4, 7 and the coordinator's Q10 note). Decisions: D-136 / ontology D-171; D-137 / ontology D-172 (Q9 lock, no Restrict); D-141 (Q10: delete the record's own uncited set deepest first, else keep and unlink, no Retire; supersedes D-137's "retire if cited"; Q11 answered: the set joins the secure family now). Current code (line refs at b046154af unless marked): RuleSetScope enum (RuleSetService.cs:21); create :387-399 and :405; ListAsync :516, GetAsync :553; AddDraftsAsync :871; CreateDraftRuleAsync :1060-1100; EditAsync :1157, new version :1277; publish :1486, scope check :1541-1555; AssignAsync :1910-1947 (Published re-scope allowed today, Retired refused :1919-1922); SetVisibilityAsync :1952; Summarize :2242; OwnerContext :2389-2393 (RequestedBy). Endpoints: RuleSetEndpoints.cs, every route behind AddFinanceAuthorizationFilter(BillingAdminAuthorization...) only; TryParseScope :227-231, :478; AssignCallers reason :770-772. At 3e11367468: RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(Entity row) (RecordOwnershipResolver.cs:336), OwnershipParentEntities (:1024), RecordReparent.SecureExitCaller (:499), IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync (:146); SecureChildReconciler.AfterRefileAsync (SecureChildReconciler.cs:849); RefileIsolationRead.BeforeWriteAsync (Services/Access/RefileIsolationRead.cs:26); the re-file precedent InvoiceDocumentRefile.cs:155, :173, :202; SecureDesignationRemoval.NotPermittedReasonCode = "sdap.unsecure.not_permitted" (:50); FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound (:293) and FinanceDenial.UniformNotFound; SecureChildLineage T("sprk_policy", "sprk_policies", ...) at :175-178; census ChildTables :47-61, RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver :127-139, entries :273-274, UnscannedWriters :306, PersonBearingWriters :2367, EveryChildTableTheServerCreatesCarriesTheCreatorPersonColumn and EveryAppCreateWriterThatActsForAPersonNamesThem; RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables (Services/Dataverse/RecordCreatorPerson.cs:78) pinned to scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables (:157) by ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchemaAgreementTests; config/secure-record-owner-role.json sprk_policy entry :281 (#2084 probe evidence, 0x80040299); SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.GuardedPrivileges (Infrastructure/Dataverse/SecureBuRoleDepthAssertion.cs:58, clause 1); RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.Ledger.cs GovernedFiles entry for Api/Finance/RuleSetEndpoints.cs (:346). Role XML: Spaarke Basic User / Core User hold prvReadsprk_ruleset at Deep (SpaarkeMaster Roles :530 / :603); prvWritesprk_ruleset (BillingAdminAuthorization.cs:29) is held through a role not in SpaarkeMaster source. uac-r2's delete design: projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/core-record-delete-design.md §1.3 and §11 (86cba5a00).</background>
