  <constraints>
    <constraint source="design note 4.1">Create, assign and publish each apply the 4.1 matrix and return 400 ruleset.invalid (publish: ruleset.publish_invalid) with the listed field errors. Record and FirmRecord need exactly one existing core lookup; ClientDefault and Firm take none. matterId, projectId and workAssignmentId are query parameters on create and on PUT /{id}/assignment (078 doctrine, RateCardImportEndpoints.cs:20-22, :166-187). The BU ids go in RuleSetAssignmentBody (AllBusinessUnits, BusinessUnitIds); each must exist.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-141 condition 3, uac-r2 review item 6">The Secure Record business unit in BusinessUnitIds is refused with field businessUnits. It is found through UAC's named resolution, SecureChildShareSynchronizer.ResolveSecureBusinessUnitAsync (Services/Access/SecureChildShareSynchronizer.cs:1233); an ambiguous or unreadable resolution refuses the write (503), never treats the list as clean. Do not resolve the business unit by a name comparison of your own.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 4.1, root CLAUDE.md section 6">Every route that NAMES a core record in the request (create, assignment) checks, as the caller, a new OperationAccessPolicy key ebilling.ruleset.scope = Read | AppendTo, through the same FinanceAuthorizationCheck Record path RateCardImportEndpoints.cs:120-133 uses (copy it; do not reuse finance.submit_invoice or finance.read). Refusal is 403 from the filter before the service runs.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 3 (REQUIREMENT), design note 4.6">Every route keyed by a rule-set id (GET /{ruleSetId}, POST /{ruleSetId}/draft, PATCH .../proposals/{policyId}, POST .../accept and .../reject, POST .../publish, PUT .../assignment, PUT .../visibility, and a retire route if one is added) reads the set's three core lookups on the server, app-only, and checks the caller's Read on that record (plus AppendTo on every write route) BEFORE anything about the set is read back or written. An unknown set id, a set the caller may not see and a set whose record the caller cannot Read all answer the SAME 404 (FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound). A ClientDefault or Firm set needs no record check. ListAsync leaves out every record-scoped set whose core record the caller cannot Read (one batched check per page). Each route's basis is declared in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (the GovernedFiles entry for Api/Finance/RuleSetEndpoints.cs). The record id is never taken from the request on these routes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-137 / ontology D-172 Q9">AssignAsync on a Published set that changes scope, firm, core record or BU list returns 409 ruleset.scope_locked ("Retire this rule set and create a new one for the new scope."), Firm sets included, and writes nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 2, design note 4.3">A Draft re-scope runs, in this order: (1) wasIsolated through RefileIsolationRead.BeforeWriteAsync before any write; (2) IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync on the SET ONLY, with RecordReparent.SecureExitCaller set for the HTTP caller (the F3 check); a refusal maps to 403 sdap.unsecure.not_permitted (SecureDesignationRemoval.NotPermittedReasonCode) and nothing else is written; (3) SecureChildReconciler.AfterRefileAsync("sprk_ruleset", id, wasIsolated, CancellationToken.None), which moves the policies and versions; do NOT reparent policies or versions one by one. Copy InvoiceDocumentRefile.cs. RuleSetService is added to RefileWriterAfterRefileGuardTests' non-vacuity list. Listed in the census UnscannedWriters as a REPARENT.</constraint>
    <constraint source="design note 4.2">The S3 flag and the N:N associate / disassociate are written as the app identity in the same call; associates are idempotent; a partial failure is 500 ruleset.write_failed. Publish re-reads the list and refuses No with an empty list. RuleSetSummary gains AllBusinessUnits, BusinessUnitIds and coreRecord {type, id, name} (additive members).</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-171 Q3, uac-r2 review item 4, design note 4.4">Owner parents come from EACH ROW'S OWN lookups: ResolveOwnerAsync(RecordOwnershipContext.ForParents(RecordOwnershipContext.ParentsOf(row), caller) with { RequestedBy = caller }) for the set (its core lookup, or none for ClientDefault / Firm), the policy (its sprk_ruleset) and the version (its sprk_policy), at create (:405), AddDraftsAsync (:871) and EditAsync (:1277). Never hand the set's core record to a policy or version create. A refusal writes nothing (409 OwnerRefused).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (binding), design note 5.1">ONE change (one PR) carries every part, because SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and the census creator-person tests fail on any subset: SecureChildLineage T("sprk_ruleset", "sprk_rulesets", ("sprk_matter", Matter), ("sprk_project", Project), ("sprk_workassignment", WorkAssignment)) and ("sprk_ruleset", "sprk_ruleset") on sprk_policy; "sprk_ruleset" in OwnershipParentEntities; the config/secure-record-owner-role.json row (logicalName sprk_ruleset, kind child, prvReadsprk_ruleset, Read, Basic, a reason and the verbatim probe evidence); sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion in RecordCreatorPerson.StampedChildTables AND in scripts/Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 $Tables (with each table's solution; ontology-r1 names it for sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion); census ChildTables + Routed entries + a PersonBearingWriters entry ("RuleSetService.cs", "OwnerContext", the billing admin who asked); the NFR-05 GuardedPrivileges entries for the three tables (schema-name casing read live).</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (live part)">The role row's evidence is a LIVE refusal probe on dev: create a sprk_ruleset row with ownerid bound to the Secure Record Owners team BEFORE the privilege is added; record the verbatim 0x80040299 refusal (the #2084 shape at config/secure-record-owner-role.json:285); if the create succeeds, delete the probe row and STOP (escalation). Then Set-SecureRecordOwnerRolePrivileges.ps1 -WhatIf, -Apply, -Verify on dev, and Set-ChildRecordCreatorPersonSchema.ps1 dry run, -Apply, -Verify on dev, each with the owner's OK. Both MUST be applied before any BFF carrying this code is deployed (079 re-verifies); otherwise every Record-scoped create on a Secure matter gets 0x80040299.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 review item 1 (NFR-05)">The depth check covers sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy and sprk_policyversion for EVERY non-admin role, including the role through which billing admins hold prvWritesprk_ruleset (read it live; it is not in SpaarkeMaster source). Record the live NFR-05 result (SecureRecordIsolationCensusJob or the manual gate) on dev in the notes. Basic and Core User hold Deep Read on sprk_ruleset and sprk_Policy, as on sprk_Matter; the live business-unit tree decides.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 Q14 condition 1 (note section 12)">In the same change: census sprk_policy / sprk_policyversion Waived → Routed, new entry ("RuleSetService.cs", "sprk_ruleset", 1, Routed), RuleSetServicePolicyWaiver deleted, sprk_ruleset in ChildTables. RuleSetServiceNoMatterScopeGuardTests replaced by the narrower guard "no sprk_matter written on a PolicyEntity or VersionEntity row". Twin guard: OntologyAdminAuthoringService never writes sprk_ruleset. Both guards have a must-fire and a must-not-fire control and a seeding proof. RuleSetServiceOwnerTests.NoWrittenPolicyOrVersionRowCarriesAMatter_OnCreateOrUpdate stays unchanged. ontology-r1 reviews both guards and the creator-person rows on its two tables.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ontology-r1 Q14 condition 2">SecureFamilyConsistencyTests and a SecureChildReconciler test cover version → policy → ruleset → core end to end, on secure and on unsecure. CitationLookups unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-141 (Q10), uac-r2 86cba5a00">No delete-Restrict and no delete code in this task: the delete job is uac-r2's. Once the citing lookups are fixed by this task's schema reading, send uac-r2 the exact list of lookups that cite the set's rows (Signal, Decision Record and invoice-side columns → sprk_policyversion / sprk_policy / sprk_ruleset), each as table.column → target, read from live metadata; their planner reads them. Do NOT send a "retire if cited" rule: D-141 has no Retire.</constraint>
    <constraint source=".claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md">BFF hygiene: placement (existing RuleSetService and endpoints), publish-size delta against a fresh master build, no new package, no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
    <constraint source="uac-r2 2026-10-20 (#2143)">Every owner write that this task routes through IRecordOwnershipResolver (create and reparent) handles the resolver's fail-closed refusal after its bounded RowVersion retries. Nothing is written, the caller gets the existing ownership-refusal error (never a 500 and never a partial write), and a test pins the refusal path. Re-read RecordOwnershipResolver.cs on origin/master before starting. If #2143 has not merged, STOP and ask the main session.</constraint>
  </constraints>

