  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any part of the secure-family change (lineage, OwnershipParentEntities, role row, creator-person rows, census, depth check) cannot land in the same PR as the others, STOP: a subset fails SecureFamilyConsistencyTests or the census, and shipping it piecemeal is what uac-r2 forbade.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the refusal probe's create SUCCEEDS (the Secure Record Owner role already reads sprk_ruleset), delete the probe row, record it and STOP: the role JSON's evidence rule cannot be met as written; ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the live NFR-05 run reports any non-admin role whose Read on sprk_ruleset, sprk_policy or sprk_policyversion reaches the Secure business unit (including the billing admins' role), STOP and raise 🔔 Human Input Required: a Secure-team owner would hide nothing, and changing a role is uac-r2's and the owner's call.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the owner has not given the OK for the probe and the two -Apply runs, do not run them; finish the code, keep the role row's evidence empty only in a local branch, do not open the PR, and report.</trigger>
    <trigger>If ontology-r1 or uac-r2 rejects a guard, the twin guard, the lineage change, the creator-person rows or the re-scope sequence in review, STOP; do not weaken a guard to make it pass.</trigger>
    <trigger>If routing through the resolver or the re-scope needs a resolver change in RecordOwnershipResolver.cs beyond adding sprk_ruleset to OwnershipParentEntities, STOP and ask uac-r2.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an id-keyed route cannot run the record check before its first read-back or write (for example a filter that has no access to the set's lookup), STOP and agree the shape with uac-r2; do not fall back to the billing-admin privilege alone.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>RuleSetService, RuleSetEndpoints and the 076 validation exist and are extended; OperationAccessPolicy has finance.read (Read) and finance.submit_invoice (Read | AppendTo) at :174 and :201; the census, SecureChildLineage, the role JSON and StampedChildTables already list sprk_policy (or its peers); the F3 re-file sequence exists in InvoiceDocumentRefile; the uniform 404 exists (FinanceAuthorizationFilter.UniformRecordNotFound).</existing>
    <extension>All behaviour extends existing files and lists. One new operation key, because neither existing key names this act (a deny would read "submit invoice", the precedent noted at OperationAccessPolicy.cs:251-253). One new guard test file and one new reconciler test file hold the two new controls.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>A matter-scoped rule set cannot be created; if it were, a caller without AppendTo could attach terms to any record, a billing admin could read or change a Secure matter's set by its id, a Draft re-scope could pull a set out of Secure without F3, a Secure matter's set, policies and versions would sit in the ordinary business unit, and every Record-scoped create on a Secure matter would fail with 0x80040299.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

